@startuml
title Coloring snapshot: consistent cut with channel state

participant Coordinator
participant P0
participant P1
participant P2

note over P0,P2
BLACK = before cut
WHITE = after cut
Initial total S = 3000
end note

== Normal traffic before snapshot ==
P0 -> P0: withdraw 700\nP0 balance = 300
P0 -[#red,dashed]> P1: Transfer(700, BLACK, null)\nnot delivered yet

== Coordinator starts snapshot ==
Coordinator -> P0: StartSnapshot(coloring-1, WHITE)
P0 -> P0: turn WHITE\nrecord balance=300
P0 --> Coordinator: LocalState(P0, 300)

P0 -> P2: Transfer(50, WHITE, coloring-1)

note right of P2
Variant 2:
WHITE transfer is implicit
(state?, WHITE).
P2 turns WHITE before processing it.
end note
P2 -> P2: turn WHITE\nrecord balance=1000\nthen deposit 50
P2 --> Coordinator: LocalState(P2, 1000)

Coordinator -> P1: StartSnapshot(coloring-1, WHITE)
P1 -> P1: turn WHITE\nrecord balance=1000
P1 --> Coordinator: LocalState(P1, 1000)

== Delayed BLACK transfer arrives ==
P0 -[#red]> P1: Transfer(700, BLACK, null)
note right of P1
P1 is already WHITE.
The BLACK transfer was sent before P0's cut
and arrived after P1's cut.
It is recorded as channel state.
end note
P1 --> Coordinator: ChannelState(P0, P1, 700)
P1 -> P1: deposit 700\nlive balance = 1700

note right of Coordinator
Snapshot total:
local states = 300 + 1000 + 1000 = 2300
channel states = 700
total = 3000 = S
end note

@enduml
